Issues Encountered & Solutions
Issue 1: Missing System Tools (node, yarn, make unrecognized)

Cause: Node.js and Yarn were not installed on the system.

Solution: Downloaded and ran the Node.js LTS installer from nodejs.org, making sure "Add to PATH" was checked.

Issue 2: Terminal environment variable caching

Cause: VS Code's embedded terminal did not recognize node immediately after running the installer.

Solution: Restarted VS Code completely to refresh system environment variables.

Issue 3: PowerShell Script Execution Security Policy (PSSecurityException)

Cause: Windows default security blocked npm.ps1 from running in PowerShell (npm install -g yarn).

Solution: Switched the VS Code terminal profile from PowerShell to Command Prompt (cmd), which bypasses PowerShell execution policies.

Issue 4: Unmet peer dependency and version resolution warnings during yarn

Cause: Radix UI sub-packages flagged missing React 19 peer dependencies and strip-ansi resolution mismatches.

Solution: Evaluated warnings as non-breaking monorepo peer notices and proceeded—no intervention required.

